# 📘 Day 6 Notes (Important Topics Only)

## HTML (HyperText Markup Language)

* Defines the **structure** of a webpage.
* HTML is **not** responsible for styling (CSS) or interactivity (JavaScript).

---

## Basic HTML Structure

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title></title>
</head>
<body>

</body>
</html>
```

* `<head>` → Metadata (title, CSS, scripts, meta tags)
* `<body>` → Everything visible on the webpage

---

## Important HTML Tags

| Tag             | Purpose          |
| --------------- | ---------------- |
| `<h1>`          | Main heading     |
| `<p>`           | Paragraph        |
| `<a>`           | Hyperlink        |
| `<img>`         | Image            |
| `<div>`         | Block container  |
| `<span>`        | Inline container |
| `<form>`        | User input form  |
| `<input>`       | Input field      |
| `<button>`      | Button           |
| `<ul>` / `<ol>` | Lists            |
| `<li>`          | List item        |

---

## Important Attributes

| Attribute     | Purpose                       |
| ------------- | ----------------------------- |
| `href`        | Link destination              |
| `src`         | Image/resource location       |
| `alt`         | Alternative text              |
| `id`          | Unique identifier             |
| `class`       | Reusable identifier           |
| `type`        | Input type                    |
| `name`        | Parameter name sent to server |
| `placeholder` | Hint text                     |
| `value`       | Default/submitted value       |

---

## ID vs Class

```text
